course: dictionary
lesson: 1658
title: Chirp: a small sound, a bright voice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Chirp means to make a short, high sound, like a small bird or a cricket. A chirp is that sound, so chirp can be a doing word or a naming word. Look at this: «Scientists found rats make high chirps when tickled.» The word chirps names the sounds, so here it is a naming word.
explain: The words around chirp give you clues. «A single short chirp every minute or so from a smoke alarm usually means its battery is low.» The words short, every minute and battery tell you the chirp is a small warning sound, not a bird song. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Chirp can also describe a voice. The phrase a cheerful chirp means a bright, happy little voice. Cheerful is the clue: when someone chirps in a cheerful way, they are speaking brightly and happily, not making a bird sound at all.
fact: Chirp means to make a short, high sound, like a small bird or a cricket.
fact: A chirp is that sound: «Otters keep in touch with squeaks, chirps and whistles.»
fact: Pumas, also called cougars or mountain lions, can chirp, but they cannot roar.
fact: «A single short chirp every minute or so from a smoke alarm usually means its battery is low.»
fact: Chirp can also mean to say something in a bright, cheerful voice, as in a cheerful chirp.
exercise: «Scientists found rats make high chirps when tickled.» In this sentence, what are the chirps? | Smoke alarms that need new batteries | Bright, cheerful voices | *Short, high sounds | Long, low growls
exercise: «A single short chirp every minute or so from a smoke alarm usually means its battery is low.» What does the chirp usually warn you about? | A new alarm that was just fitted | *The battery is low | It is time for dinner
exercise: A friend says, «She gave a cheerful chirp when she saw us.» What does cheerful chirp suggest? | A loud crash of thunder | A sad, quiet whisper | *A bright, happy voice
test: «Pumas, also called cougars or mountain lions, chirp, hiss, purr and scream but cannot roar.» Which sound can pumas NOT make? | Chirp | Hiss | Purr | *Roar
test: Which word is a doing word in this sentence? «The crickets chirp all night long.» | long | *chirp | crickets | night
exam: Jayden reads «Otters keep in touch with squeaks, chirps and whistles» and does not know what squeaks means. What helps him most? | Squeaks means the same as otters, so it is another animal | *The other words in the list are all sounds, so squeaks is probably a small sound too | He should stop reading the whole sentence | Squeaks are a kind of fish, so they must be food
